// hola.psc - Hello World in PSeInt pseudocode (Spanish keywords)
// Comments start with // and run to the end of the line, as in C++ or Java.

// An algorithm starts with the keyword Algoritmo ("algorithm") and a name.
// PSeInt also accepts Proceso ... FinProceso ("process") for the same thing.
// There is no main function, no import and no class: the steps between
// Algoritmo and FinAlgoritmo run from top to bottom.
// Keywords are not case-sensitive: algoritmo and ALGORITMO work too.
Algoritmo HolaMundo
    // Escribir ("write") prints its value and then a line break, like
    // Python's print. Text goes between double quotes. The ; at the end is
    // optional with the default settings; a teacher can choose a stricter
    // "profile" in which it is required.
    Escribir "Hello, World!";
// FinAlgoritmo ("end algorithm") closes the block opened by Algoritmo,
// like "end" in Pascal or a closing } in C.
FinAlgoritmo
